  "result": "I wrote the rule and the witnesses, but they haven't been tested: every gate run returned SCOPE_VIOLATION. The gate never got as far as building or evaluating my two files.\n\n**Why the gate fails:** its scope check flags files under `.runtime/tmp/claude-154266/…`, not my files. These are the output files from this session's shell calls (including the gate call itself), the same kind of files from other coding sessions running at the same time, and a cache-state file. Each gate call creates a new one of these files, so a rerun can't pass the check. The scope check needs to ignore `.runtime/`, and this result should be treated as an infrastructure failure.\n\n**My mistakes:** I used 4 of the 6 runs. Run 1 was premature: I called the gate before editing anything. Runs 2 and 3 were also mine: I ran the gate command by mistake, with its output thrown away, when I meant to read Core files. Run 4, on the finished files, hit the same scope violation. I didn't use the last two runs because they can't pass either. The harness will rerun the gate on the files as they are.\n\n**What I wrote:**\n- **Rule:**\n  - **Applicability:** the district assumption holds; the subject is a vehicle; it occupies a roadway r; and it is emerging onto r. Emerging means it occupies a driveway entrance or alley d and has stayed on d since a moment when it was on d and not on r.\n  - **Obligation:** it repeats that whole choice of r. For every other vehicle on r, the subject must not be moving faster than `p.halt_speed_tolerance` while their closest approach within `p.conflict_horizon` comes under `p.conflict_centre_clearance`, and it must never touch that vehicle.\n  - **Narrowings:** none added; nothing in the node was left for me to choose.\n- **Witnesses:** the 5 planned scenarios, plus 6 extra branches so that every leaf of the formula decides at least one verdict:\n  - contact while the subject is halted;\n  - a closest approach in time but far apart;\n  - a car that isn't on the roadway;\n  - a bicycle, which isn't a vehicle under the definition;\n  - outside a district;\n  - emerging from an alley.\n\nThe full run log and reasoning are in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
